<title>UK: UK output prices up 0.4% in Sept.</title>
<headline>UK output prices up 0.4% in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics (ONS) released the following provisional data on UK input and output prices in September. (Prev data in brackets)</p>
<p> OUTPUT PRICES (unadj)	   SEPT	AUGUST (PREL AUG)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.4	 UNCH	(UNCH)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			2.2	 2.0	  (2.0)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 124.0     123.5    (123.5)</p>
<p>OUTPUT PRICES EX FOOD/DRINK/TOBACCO/PETROLEUM (unadj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.1	 UNCH	(UNCH)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			0.9*	1.2	  (1.2)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 119.8     119.7    (119.7)</p>
<p>OUTPUT PRICES EX-FOOD/DRINK/TOBACCO/PETROLEUM (adj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.1	 UNCH	(UNCH)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			0.9	 1.3	  (1.3)</p>
<p> Qtr/qtr change		    UNCH	0.1	  (0.1)</p>
<p> Qtr/qtr annual rate	     UNCH**    0.2	  (0.2)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 119.9     119.8    (119.8)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES (MATERIALS AND FUEL) (unadj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.5	 -0.5	(-0.3)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change		     -2.7	 -2.5	(-2.1)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 111.6     111.0    (111.5)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES (MATERIALS AND FUEL) (adj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.3	 0.1	  (0.3)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change		     -2.9	-2.6	(-2.2)</p>
<p> Index				 113.1     112.8    (113.2)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES EX F, D, T, P (unadj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.3	 UNCH	(UNCH)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change		     -6.5	-6.8	 (-6.6)</p>
<p> Index				 107.2     106.9    (107.1)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES EX F, D, T, P (adj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.1	 0.2	  (0.1)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change		     -6.5	-6.7	 (-6.6)</p>
<p> Index				 108.1     108.0     (108.2)</p>
<p> INPUT COMPONENTS PCT CHANGE   SEPT M/M	    SEPT Y/Y</p>
<p> Fuel				   1.1		     -5.1</p>
<p> Crude oil etc			7.0		     31.8</p>
<p> Metals				-0.8		    -13.2</p>
<p> Chemicals			   -0.4		     -6.8</p>
<p> Materials: home produced	 0.1		     -1.7</p>
<p>		imported	     -1.6			0.3</p>
<p> Other home produced	     -0.8			1.5</p>
<p> Other imported materials	-0.2		     -6.9</p>
<p>Consensus of economists forecasts was for input prices to rise a seasonally adjusted 0.5 percent in September and fall 2.4 percent year-on-year. Output prices are forecast up 0.1 percent and 1.8 percent higher year-on-year.</p>
<p>* Year-on-year rise in unadjusted core output prices, of 0.9 percent, is the lowest since September 1967.</p>
<p>** Unchanged three month on three month annual rate of core output prices is the lowest rate since April 1973.</p>
<p>The ONS said crude oil prices in September were at their highest level since the Gulf War.</p>
